--- !u!114 &532182381
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 532182377}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 08344a0833919684488a444fcb701dfe, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  potentialStrings:
  - Hitting objects at fast speeds is not recommended. However, is possible.
  - DO NOT attempt to drift around corners even if it is faster than driving.
  - It never hurts to go over the quota limit.
  - Buttons can be useful to activate parts of the warehouse.
  - Do NOT attempt to carry other players.
  - Do NOT attempt to carry more than 1 crate.
  - The second floor is higher then the first, so the best crates are stored there.
  - Surprisingly, hitting a crate at fast speeds can break it. Who would have thought.
  - "\u201CPlease stop knocking over the cones\u201D \u2013 Janitor."
  - The Elevator has a 1 forklift weight limit.
  - "Quotas don\u2019t last forever, so don\u2019t forget to check their timers."
  - Call for assistance from a colleague if you need to reach high places.
  - Teamwork can be the most effective strategy to achieving high scores.
  - "Forklifts are more durable than you would think, but don\u2019t test it. "
  - Your contract states you must work 3 quotas a day or immediate termination.
  - There is a mandated speed limit, DO NOT GO OVER.
  - "If another forklift attempts to carry you, you may break free and in-act Section
    9.1 of the \u201CLegalised 1 on 1 blue collar\u201D act."
  - Not many people know this, but once you are in the forklift, YOU CAN NEVER GET
    OUT.
  - Remember, forklift arms can move up and down when the associated button is pressed.
  - "Crates come with various values, don\u2019t forget to check them. "
